  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid RezdiffraTM (resmetirom), effective 2026-06-01. Approval criteria and other liver disease denial encoded; supporting chart notes and test evidence require manual review.",
    "Limitations of use: avoid use in decompensated cirrhosis. Accelerated approval based on improvement of NASH and fibrosis; continued approval may depend on confirmatory clinical benefit trials.",
    "Cautions (notes only): cholelithiasis and cholecystitis; monitor for signs and symptoms of hepatotoxicity. Common adverse reactions include diarrhea, pruritus, nausea and abdominal pain.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months. Manual review required.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 30 tablets per 30 days; maximum 100 mg/day. Manual review required."
  ],
